            %p
              which holds by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            %p The other claims follow similarly.
          %h2#ModalTypeTheory Modal type theory
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            for bireflection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modalities"} modalities
            has been proposed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RFL21"} Riley, Finster &amp; Licata (2021)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Riley22"} Riley (2022)
          %p
            We show the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            which these authors propose to add to plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+type+theory"} intuitionistic type theory
            for encoding the presence of a bireflection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+modality"} classical modality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \natural
            on the type system, and we show corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagrams"} commuting diagrams
            in an interpreting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
            (a more syntactic semantics is indicated in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RFL21"} RFL21, Sec. 7, esp. Fig. 6
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Given a bireflection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♮
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \natural \colon \mathcal{B} \to \mathcal{B}
              as above, then for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \in \mathcal{B}
              we obtain a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            #eq:TheMonadOnSlices.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♮
                      %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Γ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\natural_\Gamma
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathcal{B}_{/\Gamma} \to \mathcal{B}_{/\Gamma}
            %p by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♮
                      %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ♮
                    %msup
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ♮
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♮
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ♮
                                    %msub
                                      %mi p
                                      %mi A
                        %mtr
